(function(E){ const x = E["hr-m5"] = E["hr-m5"] || {units:{}}; x.units["hr-5-3"] = {"explain":{"id":"c-hr-5-3-e","course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-3","type":"explain","level":"B1","title":{"en":"The appraisal meeting","tr":"Değerlendirme görüşmesi","fa":"جلسه‌ی ارزیابی عملکرد"},"objective":{"en":"After this lesson, you can run an appraisal meeting: achievements, one area to improve and the next steps.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda bir performans değerlendirme görüşmesi yürütebileceksin: başarılar, gelişecek bir alan ve sonraki adımlar.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی جلسه‌ی ارزیابی عملکرد را پیش ببری: دستاوردها، یک زمینه برای بهتر شدن و قدم‌های بعدی."},"hook":{"en":"Give evidence, then listen. People leave an appraisal knowing how they are doing, so it must be fair and two-way. 'Since April you have completed 410 deliveries.' Six months of work, still counting, in one tense.","tr":"Önce kanıt ver, sonra dinle. İnsanlar değerlendirme görüşmesinden nasıl gittiklerini öğrenerek çıkar; bu yüzden görüşme adil ve karşılıklı olmalı. 'Since April you have completed 410 deliveries.' Hâlâ süren altı aylık emek, tek bir zamanda.","fa":"مدرک بده و بعد گوش کن. آدم‌ها از جلسه‌ی ارزیابی عملکرد با تصویری از وضع کارشان بیرون می‌آیند، پس این جلسه باید منصفانه و دوطرفه باشد. «⁨Since April you have completed 410 deliveries.⁩» شش ماه کار که هنوز ادامه دارد، در یک زمان."},"before":{"en":"Write a short appraisal summary: two achievements, one area to develop and the employee’s own plan.","tr":"Kısa bir performans değerlendirme özeti yaz: iki başarı, geliştirilecek bir alan ve çalışanın kendi planı.","fa":"یک خلاصه‌ی کوتاه ارزیابی عملکرد بنویس: دو موفقیت، یک زمینه برای پیشرفت و برنامه‌ی خود کارمند."},"rounds":[[1,4],[2,3]],"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Key points","tr":"Ana nokta","fa":"نکته‌ی اصلی"},"value":"4"},{"label":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifade","fa":"عبارت کلیدی"},"value":"3"},{"label":{"en":"Practice tasks","tr":"Alıştırma","fa":"تمرین"},"value":"5"}],"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"The skill","tr":"Beceri","fa":"مهارت"},"head":{"en":"Evidence first, then their voice","tr":"Önce kanıt, sonra onların sözü","fa":"اول مدرک، بعد حرف خودش"},"body":{"en":"Start with real achievements, then one clear area to improve. Then stop talking and ask about their plans, so the meeting is two-way.","tr":"Gerçek başarılarla başla, sonra geliştirilecek tek bir alanı söyle. Ardından konuşmayı bırak ve planlarını sor; böylece görüşme karşılıklı olur.","fa":"با دستاوردهای واقعی شروع کن و بعد یک زمینه‌ی روشن برای بهتر شدن بگو. بعد خودت کمتر حرف بزن و درباره‌ی برنامه‌هایش بپرس تا جلسه دوطرفه باشد."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The language","tr":"Dil","fa":"زبان"},"head":{"en":"Achievements and contrast: present perfect, although, however","tr":"Başarılar ve karşıtlık: present perfect, although, however","fa":"دستاورد و تضاد: حال کامل، although، however"},"steps":[{"en":"A period up to now (since, this year): present perfect.","tr":"Bugüne uzanan bir dönem (since, this year): present perfect.","fa":"برای دوره‌ای که تا حالا ادامه دارد (since، this year)، حال کامل می‌آید.","ex":"Since April you have completed 410 deliveries."},{"en":"Although + clause, main clause: one sentence.","tr":"Although + yan cümle, ana cümle: tek cümle.","fa":"Although یک جمله می‌گیرد و بعدش جمله‌ی اصلی می‌آید؛ همه در یک جمله.","ex":"Although April was difficult, you have improved a lot."},{"en":"However starts a new sentence, then a comma.","tr":"However yeni bir cümle başlatır, ardından virgül gelir.","fa":"However جمله‌ی تازه را شروع می‌کند و بعدش ویرگول می‌آید.","ex":"April was difficult. However, you have improved a lot."}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Use","Example"],"tr":["Kullanım","Örnek"],"fa":["کاربرد","مثال"]},"rows":[["Achievement over a period","Since April you have completed 410 deliveries."],["Contrast in one sentence","Although April was difficult, you have improved since May."],["Contrast across two sentences","April was difficult. However, you have improved since May."]]},"tip":{"en":"Persian ba inke works like although and ba in hal like however; Turkish yine de also starts a new sentence. The usual slip is using however like although, inside one sentence. However needs its own sentence and a comma.","tr":"Türkçedeki 'ama' ve 'yine de' iki yerde de kullanılabilir; bu yüzden although ile however aynı gibi gelir. İngilizcede however kendi cümlesini ve bir virgül ister.","fa":"در فارسی «با اینکه» مثل although است و «با این حال» مثل however. «با این حال» هم مثل however معمولاً جمله‌ی تازه شروع می‌کند."},"wrong":"April was difficult, however you have improved.","right":"April was difficult. However, you have improved since May."},{"eyebrow":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های کلیدی"},"head":{"en":"Phrases for this task","tr":"Bu görev için ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های این کار"},"phrases":[{"phrase":"Since April you have...","meaning":{"en":"Names achievements over the period.","tr":"Dönem boyunca başarıları sayar.","fa":"دستاوردهای این دوره را می‌گوید."}},{"phrase":"What would you like to do next year?","meaning":{"en":"An open question about plans.","tr":"Planlar hakkında açık soru.","fa":"یک سؤال باز درباره‌ی برنامه‌های آینده."}},{"phrase":"You hesitated there. Is there something you'd like to add?","meaning":{"en":"Gently invites what was not said.","tr":"Söylenmeyeni nazikçe davet eder.","fa":"با ملایمت، فرد را به گفتن ناگفته‌ها دعوت می‌کند."}}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"At work","tr":"İş yerinde","fa":"در محیط کار"},"head":{"en":"Make ambition safe to say","tr":"İsteklerini söylemeyi kolaylaştır","fa":"کاری کن راحت از خواسته‌هایش حرف بزند"},"body":{"en":"In many UK and US companies the employee writes a self-assessment before the appraisal and is expected to talk about their own ambitions. In many workplaces in Turkey, Iran and the Persian Gulf, asking a manager for more responsibility can feel disloyal or pushy, especially with the manager present. A good appraiser asks open questions and makes it safe to say \"I would like to...\".","tr":"Birçok İngiliz ve Amerikan şirketinde çalışan, değerlendirmeden önce bir öz değerlendirme yazar ve kendi hedeflerinden bahsetmesi beklenir. Türkiye, İran ve Basra Körfezi'ndeki birçok işyerinde bir yöneticiden daha fazla sorumluluk istemek, özellikle yönetici oradayken, sadakatsizlik ya da ısrarcılık gibi gelebilir. İyi bir değerlendirici açık sorular sorar ve \"I would like to...\" demeyi güvenli hâle getirir.","fa":"در بسیاری از شرکت‌های بریتانیا و آمریکا، کارمند پیش از جلسه‌ی ارزیابی یک خودارزیابی می‌نویسد و از او انتظار می‌رود درباره‌ی آرزوهای شغلی‌اش حرف بزند. در بسیاری از محیط‌های کاری ترکیه، ایران و کشورهای حاشیه‌ی خلیج فارس، اینکه کسی از مدیرش مسئولیت بیشتری بخواهد، به‌خصوص در حضور خود مدیر، ممکن است نوعی بی‌وفایی یا پررویی به نظر برسد. ارزیاب خوب سؤال باز می‌پرسد و فضایی می‌سازد که گفتن «⁨I would like to...⁩» بی‌خطر باشد."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"From weak to strong","tr":"Zayıftan güçlüye","fa":"از قضاوت تا مدرک و سؤال"},"text":"Facts: 200 cases closed since June. Reports often arrive late.","item":"Overall you're fine. Just be more careful. Sign here.","why":{"en":"Weak: a judgement, with no evidence. Strong: a number, one area, one question.","tr":"Zayıf: kanıtsız bir yargı. Güçlü: bir sayı, bir alan, bir soru.","fa":"نسخه‌ی اول قضاوتی بدون مدرک است. نسخه‌ی دوم یک عدد، یک زمینه‌ی بهبود و یک سؤال دارد."},"answer":"Since June you have closed 200 cases. Your reports often arrive late. What would you like to do next year?","cut":["Overall you're fine.","Just be more careful.","Sign here."],"cutHint":{"en":"Tap what gives no evidence and leaves the employee no voice.","tr":"Hiç kanıt vermeyen ve çalışana söz hakkı bırakmayan şeylere dokun.","fa":"روی چیزهایی بزن که هیچ شاهدی نمی‌دهند و فرصت حرف زدن را از کارمند می‌گیرند."}},"quick":{"prompt":"Before an appraisal in many UK and US companies, what does the employee usually do?","options":["Write a self-assessment","Nothing: the manager does it all","Choose their own pay rise"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Write a self-assessment, and talk about their own ambitions. In other workplaces this can feel pushy, so ask open questions.","tr":"Bir öz değerlendirme yazar ve kendi hedeflerinden söz eder. Başka iş yerlerinde bu fazla iddialı görünebilir; bu yüzden açık uçlu sorular sor.","fa":"یک خودارزیابی می‌نویسد و درباره‌ی هدف‌های خودش حرف می‌زند. در بعضی محیط‌ها این کار ممکن است زیاده‌خواهی به نظر برسد، پس سؤال باز بپرس."},"point":4,"hint2":{"en":"Think about what the employee brings to the meeting so that their own view is on the table from the start.","tr":"Çalışanın kendi görüşünün baştan masada olması için toplantıya ne getirdiğini düşün.","fa":"فکر کن کارمند چه چیزی با خودش به جلسه می‌آورد تا نظر خودش از اول روی میز باشد."}},"remember":{"en":"Can you put a full stop before the contrast word? Then use However. If not, use although. Result of this lesson: you can run a two-way appraisal. You also have the written summary.","tr":"Zıtlık kelimesinden önce nokta koyabiliyor musun? O zaman However. Koyamıyorsan although. Bu dersin sonucu: karşılıklı bir değerlendirme görüşmesi yapabilirsin ve elinde yazılı özeti olur.","fa":"می‌توانی پیش از کلمه‌ی تضاد نقطه بگذاری؟ پس However. اگر نه، ⁨although⁩. حالا می‌توانی جلسه‌ی ارزیابی دوطرفه‌ای برگزار کنی. خلاصه‌ی نوشته‌شده‌اش هم آماده است."},"b2Point":{"eyebrow":{"en":"B2 track","tr":"B2 yolu","fa":"مسیر B2"},"head":{"en":"Inviting agreement: tags with falling tone, negative questions","tr":"Onaya davet etmek: düşen tonlu onay soruları (question tags), olumsuz sorular","fa":"دعوت به موافقت: question tag با لحن پایین‌رونده، سؤال منفی"},"steps":[{"en":"Falling tone on the tag: you expect a yes.","tr":"Onay sorusunda düşen ton: 'evet' bekliyorsun.","fa":"لحن پایین‌رونده روی tag یعنی انتظار «بله» داری.","ex":"You've really enjoyed the new route, haven't you?"},{"en":"Negative questions invite agreement gently.","tr":"Olumsuz sorular nazikçe onaya davet eder.","fa":"سؤال منفی با ملایمت به موافقت دعوت می‌کند.","ex":"Wouldn't you say the reports are easier now?"},{"en":"Never a tag after a question; match the tag to the verb.","tr":"Sorudan sonra onay sorusu gelmez; onay sorusunu fiile uydur.","fa":"بعد از سؤال tag نمی‌آید؛ tag را با فعل هماهنگ کن.","ex":"The new route is better, isn't it?"}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Pattern","Example","Tone"],"tr":["Kalıp","Örnek","Ton"],"fa":["الگو","مثال","لحن"]},"rows":[["Tag inviting agreement","You've enjoyed the new route, haven't you?","falling"],["Real question tag","You haven't sent the report yet, have you?","rising"],["Negative question","Wouldn't you say the reports are easier now?","falling"]]},"body":{"en":"B2 track: in the appraisal, use one falling-tone tag and one negative question to invite agreement, then one fully open question.","tr":"B2 yolu: değerlendirmede onay davet etmek için düşen tonlu bir onay sorusu ve bir olumsuz soru, sonra da tamamen açık bir soru kullan.","fa":"مسیر B2: در جلسه‌ی ارزیابی، یک tag با لحن پایین‌رونده و یک سؤال منفی برای دعوت به موافقت به کار ببر و بعد یک سؤال کاملاً باز بپرس."}}},"grammar":{"id":"c-hr-5-3-g","level":"B1","course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-3","title":"Achievements and contrast: present perfect, although, however","titleTr":"Başarılar ve karşıtlık: present perfect, although, however","exp":{"en":"An appraisal looks back over a period that continues to now, so achievements take the present perfect: \"Since April you have completed 410 deliveries.\", \"Your late deliveries have gone down to one a month.\" With since, for or \"this year\" do not use the past simple: not \"Since April you completed\". To balance good news and a development point, use contrast. Although joins two ideas in one sentence: \"Although April was difficult, you have improved a lot since May.\" However starts a new sentence and is followed by a comma: \"April was difficult. However, you have improved a lot since May.\" Do not use however like although (\"However April was difficult, you...\" is wrong).","tr":"Performans değerlendirmesi şimdiye kadar süren bir döneme bakar, bu yüzden başarılar present perfect alır: \"Since April you have completed 410 deliveries.\", \"Your late deliveries have gone down to one a month.\" Since, for ya da \"this year\" ile past simple kullanma: \"Since April you completed\" değil. İyi haberi ve gelişim noktasını dengelemek için karşıtlık kullan. Although iki fikri tek cümlede birleştirir: \"Although April was difficult, you have improved a lot since May.\" However yeni bir cümle başlatır ve ardından virgül gelir: \"April was difficult. However, you have improved a lot since May.\" However'ı although gibi kullanma (\"However April was difficult, you...\" yanlıştır).","fa":"جلسه‌ی ارزیابی عملکرد به دوره‌ای نگاه می‌کند که تا امروز ادامه دارد؛ پس دستاوردها را با حال کامل می‌گوییم: «⁨Since April you have completed 410 deliveries.⁩» و «⁨Your late deliveries have gone down to one a month.⁩» با since، for یا this year از گذشته‌ی ساده استفاده نکن: نه «Since April you completed». برای اینکه خبر خوب و نکته‌ی قابل‌بهبود را متعادل کنی، از کلمه‌های تضاد کمک بگیر. although دو ایده را در یک جمله به هم وصل می‌کند (مثل «با اینکه»): «⁨Although April was difficult, you have improved a lot since May.⁩» اما however یک جمله‌ی تازه را شروع می‌کند و بعدش ویرگول می‌آید (مثل «با این حال»): «⁨April was difficult. However, you have improved a lot since May.⁩» however را جای although به کار نبر: «⁨However April was difficult, you...⁩» غلط است."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Use","Example"],"tr":["Kullanım","Örnek"],"fa":["کاربرد","مثال"]},"rows":[["Achievement over a period","Since April you have completed 410 deliveries."],["Contrast in one sentence","Although April was difficult, you have improved since May."],["Contrast across two sentences","April was difficult. However, you have improved since May."]]},"wrong":"However April was difficult, you have improved a lot since May.","right":"Although April was difficult, you have improved a lot since May.","blank":{"sentence":"___ April was difficult, you have improved a lot since May.","word":"Although","distractors":["However","Despite"]},"wrong2":"Since April you completed 410 deliveries.","right2":"Since April you have completed 410 deliveries.","blank2":{"sentence":"Since April you ___ 410 deliveries.","word":"have completed","distractors":["completed","are completing"]},"expParts":{"tryFrom":"blank","hook":{"en":"'Since April you have completed 410 deliveries.' Six months of work, still counting, in one tense.","tr":"'Since April you have completed 410 deliveries.' Hâlâ süren altı aylık emek, tek bir zamanda.","fa":"«⁨Since April you have completed 410 deliveries.⁩» شش ماه کار که هنوز ادامه دارد، در یک زمان."},"tryWhy":{"en":"Although: it joins two ideas in one sentence. However starts a new sentence, and Despite needs a noun.","tr":"Although: iki fikri tek cümlede birleştirir. However yeni bir cümle başlatır, Despite ise isim ister.","fa":"جواب Although است: دو فکر را در یک جمله به هم وصل می‌کند. However جمله‌ی تازه شروع می‌کند و Despite اسم می‌خواهد."},"rule":[{"en":"A period up to now (since, this year): present perfect.","tr":"Bugüne uzanan bir dönem (since, this year): present perfect.","fa":"برای دوره‌ای که تا حالا ادامه دارد (since، this year)، حال کامل می‌آید.","ex":"Since April you have completed 410 deliveries."},{"en":"Although + clause, main clause: one sentence.","tr":"Although + yan cümle, ana cümle: tek cümle.","fa":"Although یک جمله می‌گیرد و بعدش جمله‌ی اصلی می‌آید؛ همه در یک جمله.","ex":"Although April was difficult, you have improved a lot."},{"en":"However starts a new sentence, then a comma.","tr":"However yeni bir cümle başlatır, ardından virgül gelir.","fa":"However جمله‌ی تازه را شروع می‌کند و بعدش ویرگول می‌آید.","ex":"April was difficult. However, you have improved a lot."}],"test":{"en":"Can you put a full stop before the contrast word? Then use However. If not, use although.","tr":"Zıtlık kelimesinden önce nokta koyabiliyor musun? O zaman However. Koyamıyorsan although.","fa":"می‌توانی پیش از کلمه‌ی تضاد نقطه بگذاری؟ پس However. اگر نه، ⁨although⁩."},"contrast":{"en":"Persian ba inke works like although and ba in hal like however; Turkish yine de also starts a new sentence. The usual slip is using however like although, inside one sentence. However needs its own sentence and a comma.","tr":"Türkçedeki 'ama' ve 'yine de' iki yerde de kullanılabilir; bu yüzden although ile however aynı gibi gelir. İngilizcede however kendi cümlesini ve bir virgül ister.","fa":"در فارسی «با اینکه» مثل although است و «با این حال» مثل however. «با این حال» هم مثل however معمولاً جمله‌ی تازه شروع می‌کند."}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["however april","however it was","however the","however he","however you"],"fix":{"en":"However starts a new sentence and takes a comma: 'April was difficult. However, ...' Or use although.","tr":"However yeni bir cümle başlatır ve virgül alır: 'April was difficult. However, ...' Ya da although kullan.","fa":"However جمله‌ی تازه را شروع می‌کند و ویرگول می‌گیرد: «⁨April was difficult. However, ...⁩» یا از although استفاده کن."}},{"find":["since april you completed","since april he completed","since may you improved","since april deniz completed","this year you completed"],"fix":{"en":"With since or this year use the present perfect: 'Since April you have completed...'","tr":"since ya da this year ile present perfect kullan: 'Since April you have completed...'","fa":"با since یا this year حال کامل بیاور: «⁨Since April you have completed...⁩»"}}]},"b2":{"id":"c-hr-5-3-b2","level":"B2","track":"B2","course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-3","title":"Inviting agreement: tags with falling tone, negative questions","titleTr":"Onaya davet etmek: düşen tonlu onay soruları (question tags), olumsuz sorular","exp":{"en":"In unit 1.4 you built question tags. In an appraisal you can use them to invite agreement, not to ask for information. Say the tag with a falling tone when you expect a yes: \"You've really enjoyed the new route, haven't you?\" (falling = \"I think so, do you agree?\"). A rising tone sounds like a real question. Negative questions do a similar job: \"Wouldn't you say the reports are easier now?\", \"Don't you think Friday works better?\" Use them gently: too many sound like pressure. Two traps: never put a tag after a question (\"Don't you think..., isn't it?\"), and match the tag to the verb: \"The new route is better, isn't it?\", not \"doesn't it?\".","tr":"1.4. derste onay sorularını (question tags) kurdun. Değerlendirme görüşmesinde onları bilgi istemek için değil, onay davet etmek için kullanabilirsin. Evet beklediğinde onay sorusunu düşen bir tonla söyle: \"You've really enjoyed the new route, haven't you?\" (düşen ton = \"bence öyle, katılıyor musun?\"). Yükselen ton gerçek bir soru gibi duyulur. Olumsuz sorular da benzer bir iş görür: \"Wouldn't you say the reports are easier now?\", \"Don't you think Friday works better?\" Bunları nazikçe kullan; fazlası baskı gibi gelir. İki tuzak: bir sorudan sonra asla onay sorusu koyma (\"Don't you think..., isn't it?\") ve onay sorusunu fiile uydur: \"The new route is better, isn't it?\", \"doesn't it?\" değil.","fa":"در درس ۱.۴ ساختن question tag را یاد گرفتی. در جلسه‌ی ارزیابی می‌توانی از آن برای دعوت به موافقت استفاده کنی، نه برای گرفتن اطلاعات. وقتی انتظار جواب «بله» داری، tag را با لحن پایین‌رونده بگو: «⁨You've really enjoyed the new route, haven't you?⁩» (لحن پایین‌رونده یعنی «فکر می‌کنم همین‌طور است، موافقید؟»). اگر لحن بالارونده باشد، مثل یک سؤال واقعی شنیده می‌شود. سؤال‌های منفی هم همین کار را می‌کنند: «⁨Wouldn't you say the reports are easier now?⁩» و «⁨Don't you think Friday works better?⁩» با احتیاط از آن‌ها استفاده کن؛ زیادی‌اش حس فشار می‌دهد. دو تله: بعد از یک سؤال هیچ‌وقت tag نگذار («⁨Don't you think..., isn't it?⁩»)، و tag را با فعل جمله جور کن: «⁨The new route is better, isn't it?⁩»، نه «⁨doesn't it?⁩»."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Pattern","Example","Tone"],"tr":["Kalıp","Örnek","Ton"],"fa":["الگو","مثال","لحن"]},"rows":[["Tag inviting agreement","You've enjoyed the new route, haven't you?","falling"],["Real question tag","You haven't sent the report yet, have you?","rising"],["Negative question","Wouldn't you say the reports are easier now?","falling"]]},"wrong":"The new route is better, doesn't it?","right":"The new route is better, isn't it?","blank":{"sentence":"You've really enjoyed the new route, ___?","word":"haven't you","distractors":["didn't you","isn't it"]},"wrong2":"Don't you think the reports are easier now, isn't it?","right2":"Don't you think the reports are easier now?","blank2":{"sentence":"___ you say the reports are easier now?","word":"Wouldn't","distractors":["Don't","Aren't"]},"useIn":{"en":"B2 track: in the appraisal, use one falling-tone tag and one negative question to invite agreement, then one fully open question.","tr":"B2 yolu: değerlendirmede onay davet etmek için düşen tonlu bir onay sorusu ve bir olumsuz soru, sonra da tamamen açık bir soru kullan.","fa":"مسیر B2: در جلسه‌ی ارزیابی، یک tag با لحن پایین‌رونده و یک سؤال منفی برای دعوت به موافقت به کار ببر و بعد یک سؤال کاملاً باز بپرس."},"exitItem":{"from":"hr-5-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"___ that a good result?","options":["Isn't","Doesn't","Wasn't it"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Isn't: a negative question with be invites agreement: 'Isn't that a good result?' 'Doesn't' needs a main verb, and 'Wasn't it' adds an extra it.","tr":"Isn't: be ile kurulan olumsuz soru onay ister: 'Isn't that a good result?' 'Doesn't' ana fiil ister; 'Wasn't it' fazladan bir it ekler.","fa":"Isn't درست است، چون سؤال منفی با be دعوت به موافقت است: Isn't that a good result? doesn't فعل اصلی می‌خواهد و wasn't it یک it اضافه دارد."}},"expParts":{"hook":{"en":"'You've really enjoyed the new route, haven't you?' With a falling tone it invites a yes, and a conversation.","tr":"'You've really enjoyed the new route, haven't you?' Düşen tonla söylenince bir 'evet'e ve sohbete davet eder.","fa":"«⁨You've really enjoyed the new route, haven't you?⁩» با لحن پایین‌رونده، دعوتی است به «بله» و به گفتگو."},"tryWhy":{"en":"Wouldn't: 'Wouldn't you say...?' is the fixed negative question. Don't you say and Aren't you say do not work.","tr":"Wouldn't: 'Wouldn't you say...?' kalıplaşmış bir olumsuz sorudur. Don't you say ve Aren't you say olmaz.","fa":"جواب Wouldn't است: Wouldn't you say...? یک سؤال منفیِ ثابت است. Don't you say و Aren't you say درست نیستند."},"rule":[{"en":"Falling tone on the tag: you expect a yes.","tr":"Onay sorusunda düşen ton: 'evet' bekliyorsun.","fa":"لحن پایین‌رونده روی tag یعنی انتظار «بله» داری.","ex":"You've really enjoyed the new route, haven't you?"},{"en":"Negative questions invite agreement gently.","tr":"Olumsuz sorular nazikçe onaya davet eder.","fa":"سؤال منفی با ملایمت به موافقت دعوت می‌کند.","ex":"Wouldn't you say the reports are easier now?"},{"en":"Never a tag after a question; match the tag to the verb.","tr":"Sorudan sonra onay sorusu gelmez; onay sorusunu fiile uydur.","fa":"بعد از سؤال tag نمی‌آید؛ tag را با فعل هماهنگ کن.","ex":"The new route is better, isn't it?"}],"test":{"en":"Does the sentence already start as a question (Don't you think...?)? Then delete the tag.","tr":"Cümle zaten soru olarak mı başlıyor (Don't you think...?)? O zaman onay sorusunu sil.","fa":"جمله از اول سؤالی شروع شده (Don't you think...?)؟ پس tag را پاک کن."},"contrast":{"en":"Turkish değil mi and Persian mage na never change and can follow almost any statement. In English a tag follows a statement only, and its verb must match.","tr":"Türkçedeki 'değil mi?' hiç değişmez ve hemen her düz cümlenin sonuna eklenebilir. İngilizcede onay sorusu yalnızca düz cümleden sonra gelir ve fiili cümleye uymalıdır.","fa":"«مگه نه؟» در فارسی هیچ‌وقت عوض نمی‌شود و تقریباً به آخر هر جمله‌ی خبری اضافه می‌شود. در انگلیسی tag فقط بعد از جمله‌ی خبری می‌آید و فعلش باید هماهنگ باشد."}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["easier now, isn't it","think so, isn't it","is better, doesn't it","is good, doesn't it","was good, didn't it","route, isn't it"],"fix":{"en":"Match the tag to the verb, and add no tag after a question: 'The new route is better, isn't it?'","tr":"Onay sorusunu fiile uydur ve sorudan sonra onay sorusu koyma: 'The new route is better, isn't it?'","fa":"tag را با فعل هماهنگ کن و بعد از سؤال tag نگذار: «⁨The new route is better, isn't it?⁩»"}}]},"vocab":{"id":"c-hr-5-3-v","level":"B1","category":"vocab","course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-3","goals":["career"],"title":{"en":"Appraisals","tr":"Performans Değerlendirmeleri","fa":"ارزیابی عملکرد"},"cards":[{"word":"appraisal","sentence":"Your appraisal is on 30 September.","meaning":{"en":"A meeting to review someone's work.","tr":"performans değerlendirmesi.","fa":"ارزیابی عملکرد (جلسه‌ی مرور کار یک نفر)"}},{"word":"achievement","sentence":"Let's start with your achievements.","gap":"achievements","accept":["achievements","achievement"],"meaning":{"en":"Something good you did with effort.","tr":"başarı.","fa":"دستاورد"}},{"word":"area for development","sentence":"Route reports are one area for development.","meaning":{"en":"A skill or habit to improve.","tr":"gelişim alanı.","fa":"زمینه‌ی قابل‌بهبود؛ مهارت یا عادتی که باید بهتر شود"}},{"word":"self-assessment","sentence":"Please fill in the self-assessment before the meeting.","meaning":{"en":"Your own review of your work.","tr":"öz değerlendirme.","fa":"خودارزیابی"}},{"word":"on track","sentence":"You are on track to reach all three goals.","meaning":{"en":"Making the progress you planned.","tr":"yolunda, planlandığı gibi.","fa":"طبق برنامه؛ در مسیر درست"}},{"word":"exceed expectations","sentence":"Your on-time record exceeds expectations.","gap":"exceeds expectations","accept":["exceeds expectations","exceed expectations"],"meaning":{"en":"To do better than what was asked.","tr":"beklentileri aşmak.","fa":"فراتر از انتظار عمل کردن"}},{"word":"meet expectations","sentence":"Your paperwork now meets expectations.","gap":"meets expectations","accept":["meets expectations","meet expectations"],"meaning":{"en":"To do what was asked, at the right level.","tr":"beklentileri karşılamak.","fa":"در حد انتظار عمل کردن"}},{"word":"pass probation","sentence":"I'm happy to confirm that you have passed probation.","gap":"passed probation","accept":["passed probation","pass probation"],"meaning":{"en":"To finish the test period successfully.","tr":"deneme süresini başarıyla tamamlamak.","fa":"دوره‌ی آزمایشی را با موفقیت پشت سر گذاشتن"}},{"word":"two-way","sentence":"An appraisal is a two-way conversation.","meaning":{"en":"Where both people speak and listen.","tr":"karşılıklı.","fa":"دوطرفه (هر دو طرف حرف می‌زنند و گوش می‌دهند)"}},{"word":"hesitate","sentence":"He hesitated before he answered.","gap":"hesitated","accept":["hesitated","hesitate"],"meaning":{"en":"To stop for a moment because you are unsure.","tr":"tereddüt etmek.","fa":"از سر تردید مکث کردن؛ دودل بودن"}}]},"story":{"id":"c-hr-5-3-s","level":"B1","genre":"Workplace","course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-3","title":{"en":"Six Months","tr":"Altı Ay","fa":"شش ماه"},"text":"On 30 September, Deniz joined the video call from the warehouse office. Leyla was in Istanbul and Omar was in the room next door, which meant he joined from his phone and his camera showed mostly ceiling.\n\n\"Thanks for joining,\" Leyla said. \"Today we'll look at what you've achieved, one area to develop, and your plans. It's a two-way conversation, so please interrupt me.\"\n\nShe started with the numbers. \"Since April you have completed 410 deliveries. Your late deliveries have gone down from six a month to one in September. And you have finished the defensive-driving course.\"\n\nDeniz smiled at the word one.\n\n\"One area to develop,\" she went on. \"Although your paperwork is now excellent, your route reports often arrive a day late. If they came in on Friday, Omar could plan the next week earlier.\"\n\n\"That's fair,\" Deniz said. \"Friday afternoon. I can do that.\"\n\n\"And I'm happy to confirm that you have passed probation.\"\n\nOmar's ceiling said, \"Well done.\"\n\nThen Leyla asked her last question. \"Is there anything else you'd like to say?\"\n\nDeniz had a sentence ready. He had practised it in the truck for a week: I would like to help train the new drivers. Hasan said he was good at explaining. Two of the new drivers already called him with questions.\n\nBut Omar was listening, and Omar was his manager, and asking for more felt like saying the job was not enough.\n\n\"No,\" Deniz said. \"Everything is good. Thank you.\"\n\nAfter the call he sat in the truck for a long time with the engine off, saying the sentence to the windscreen.","vocab":[{"word":"ceiling","en":"The top surface of a room.","tr":"tavan","fa":"سقف"},{"word":"interrupt","en":"To start speaking while someone else is speaking.","tr":"sözünü kesmek","fa":"وسط حرف کسی پریدن"},{"word":"practise","en":"To do something again and again to get better.","tr":"alıştırma yapmak, prova etmek","fa":"تمرین کردن"},{"word":"engine","en":"The part of a vehicle that makes it move.","tr":"motor","fa":"موتور"},{"word":"windscreen","en":"The front window of a vehicle.","tr":"ön cam","fa":"شیشه‌ی جلوی خودرو"}],"quiz":[{"prompt":"What was Deniz's area for development?","options":["Late route reports","Unsigned delivery notes","Speaking to customers"],"correct":0},{"prompt":"Choose the correct sentence.","options":["Since April you completed 410 deliveries.","Since April you have completed 410 deliveries.","Since April you are completing 410 deliveries."],"correct":1},{"prompt":"Why was Leyla's last question not enough?","options":["It was too long","It was a yes/no question, and Omar was listening","It was in the wrong tense"],"correct":1},{"prompt":"Why did Deniz not say his sentence?","options":["He forgot it","Asking for more felt like saying the job was not enough","He did not want to train anyone"],"correct":1}],"notice":{"en":"Deniz has one sentence ready, practised in the truck for a week. Watch for the moment he could say it.","tr":"Deniz'in kamyonda bir hafta boyunca prova ettiği bir cümlesi var. Onu söyleyebileceği ana dikkat et.","fa":"دنیز جمله‌ای آماده دارد که یک هفته در کامیون تمرینش کرده. دنبال لحظه‌ای بگرد که می‌توانست آن را بگوید."},"bridge":{"en":"'Since April you have completed...' and 'Although your paperwork is now excellent...' Next: see how they work.","tr":"'Since April you have completed...' ve 'Although your paperwork is now excellent...' Sırada: nasıl çalıştıklarını gör.","fa":"«⁨Since April you have completed...⁩» و «⁨Although your paperwork is now excellent...⁩» قدم بعد: ببین چطور کار می‌کنند."}},"speaking":{"id":"hr-5-3","course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-3","topic":{"en":"Running an Appraisal","tr":"Performans Değerlendirmesi Yürütmek","fa":"اداره‌ی جلسه‌ی ارزیابی عملکرد"},"warmup":{"en":"Think of a review or appraisal you had. Did you say everything you wanted to say?","tr":"Yaşadığın bir değerlendirme görüşmesini düşün. Söylemek istediğin her şeyi söyledin mi?","fa":"یکی از جلسه‌های ارزیابی خودت را به یاد بیاور. همه‌ی حرف‌هایی را که می‌خواستی زدی؟"},"questions":[{"en":"Open: purpose, the parts of the meeting, and \"it's a two-way conversation\".","tr":"Aç: amaç, toplantının aşamaları ve \"it's a two-way conversation\".","fa":"جلسه را شروع کن: هدف جلسه، بخش‌های آن و اینکه «it's a two-way conversation»."},{"en":"Give two achievements with the present perfect and one area for development with although or however.","tr":"Present perfect ile iki başarı ve although ya da however ile bir gelişim alanı söyle.","fa":"دو دستاورد را با حال کامل بگو و یک زمینه‌ی قابل‌بهبود را با although یا however."},{"en":"Ask an open question about his plans, notice any hesitation, and agree next steps.","tr":"Planları hakkında açık bir soru sor, tereddüdü fark et ve sonraki adımlar üzerinde anlaşın.","fa":"یک سؤال باز درباره‌ی برنامه‌هایش بپرس، به مکث و تردیدش دقت کن و سر قدم‌های بعدی توافق کن."}],"followups":[{"en":"Run the whole appraisal in 90 seconds, then 60, then 45.","tr":"Değerlendirmenin tamamını 90, sonra 60, sonra 45 saniyede yürüt.","fa":"کل جلسه‌ی ارزیابی را یک بار در ۹۰ ثانیه، بعد در ۶۰ و بعد در ۴۵ ثانیه اجرا کن."},{"en":"Now name one real achievement of yours this year, and one thing to improve.","tr":"Şimdi bu yılki gerçek bir başarını ve geliştirmek istediğin bir şeyi söyle.","fa":"حالا یک موفقیت واقعی امسالت و یک چیز را که باید بهترش کنی بگو."}],"expressions":[{"phrase":"Since April you have...","meaning":{"en":"Names achievements over the period.","tr":"Dönem boyunca başarıları sayar.","fa":"دستاوردهای این دوره را می‌گوید."}},{"phrase":"What would you like to do next year?","meaning":{"en":"An open question about plans.","tr":"Planlar hakkında açık soru.","fa":"یک سؤال باز درباره‌ی برنامه‌های آینده."}},{"phrase":"You hesitated there. Is there something you'd like to add?","meaning":{"en":"Gently invites what was not said.","tr":"Söylenmeyeni nazikçe davet eder.","fa":"با ملایمت، فرد را به گفتن ناگفته‌ها دعوت می‌کند."}}],"culture":{"en":"In many UK and US companies the employee writes a self-assessment before the appraisal and is expected to talk about their own ambitions. In many workplaces in Turkey, Iran and the Persian Gulf, asking a manager for more responsibility can feel disloyal or pushy, especially with the manager present. A good appraiser asks open questions and makes it safe to say \"I would like to...\".","tr":"Birçok İngiliz ve Amerikan şirketinde çalışan, değerlendirmeden önce bir öz değerlendirme yazar ve kendi hedeflerinden bahsetmesi beklenir. Türkiye, İran ve Basra Körfezi'ndeki birçok işyerinde bir yöneticiden daha fazla sorumluluk istemek, özellikle yönetici oradayken, sadakatsizlik ya da ısrarcılık gibi gelebilir. İyi bir değerlendirici açık sorular sorar ve \"I would like to...\" demeyi güvenli hâle getirir.","fa":"در بسیاری از شرکت‌های بریتانیا و آمریکا، کارمند پیش از جلسه‌ی ارزیابی یک خودارزیابی می‌نویسد و از او انتظار می‌رود درباره‌ی آرزوهای شغلی‌اش حرف بزند. در بسیاری از محیط‌های کاری ترکیه، ایران و کشورهای حاشیه‌ی خلیج فارس، اینکه کسی از مدیرش مسئولیت بیشتری بخواهد، به‌خصوص در حضور خود مدیر، ممکن است نوعی بی‌وفایی یا پررویی به نظر برسد. ارزیاب خوب سؤال باز می‌پرسد و فضایی می‌سازد که گفتن «⁨I would like to...⁩» بی‌خطر باشد."},"model":"Thanks for joining, Deniz. Today we'll look at your achievements, one area to develop, and your plans. It's a two-way conversation. Since April you have completed 410 deliveries, and your late deliveries have gone down to one a month. Although your paperwork is now excellent, your route reports often arrive late. What would you like to do next year? You hesitated there. Is there something you'd like to add?","selfCheck":[{"en":"I opened with the purpose, the parts and 'two-way conversation'.","tr":"Amaç, aşamalar ve 'two-way conversation' ile başladım.","fa":"با هدف جلسه، بخش‌هایش و «two-way conversation» شروع کردم."},{"en":"I gave achievements in the present perfect.","tr":"Başarıları present perfect ile verdim.","fa":"دستاوردها را با حال کامل گفتم."},{"en":"I balanced the development point with although or however.","tr":"Gelişim noktasını although ya da however ile dengeledim.","fa":"نکته‌ی قابل‌بهبود را با although یا however متعادل کردم."},{"en":"I asked an open question and noticed the hesitation.","tr":"Açık bir soru sordum ve tereddüdü fark ettim.","fa":"یک سؤال باز پرسیدم و مکث و تردیدش را دیدم."}]},"branch":{"id":"c-hr-5-3-b","course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-3","type":"branch","title":{"en":"The Six-Month Appraisal","tr":"Altı Aylık Değerlendirme","fa":"ارزیابی شش‌ماهه"},"setting":{"en":"A video call on 30 September. You are Leyla, running Deniz's end-of-probation appraisal in five steps: open, achievements, one development area, his view, next steps. If a choice goes badly, you will see what happens and can try again.","tr":"30 Eylül'de bir görüntülü görüşme. Sen Leyla'sın ve Deniz'in deneme süresi sonu değerlendirmesini beş adımda yürütüyorsun: açılış, başarılar, bir gelişim alanı, onun görüşü, sonraki adımlar. Bir seçim kötü giderse ne olduğunu görürsün ve yeniden deneyebilirsin.","fa":"یک تماس تصویری در ۳۰ سپتامبر. تو لیلا هستی و جلسه‌ی ارزیابی پایان دوره‌ی آزمایشی دنیز را در پنج مرحله اداره می‌کنی: شروع، دستاوردها، یک زمینه‌ی قابل‌بهبود، نظر خود دنیز و قدم‌های بعدی. اگر انتخابی خوب پیش نرود، نتیجه‌اش را می‌بینی و می‌توانی دوباره امتحان کنی."},"start":"n1","nodes":{"n1":{"speaker":"Deniz","line":"Hello. Is this my probation review?","choices":[{"text":"Yes. Thanks for joining. Today we'll look at what you've achieved, one area to develop, and your plans. It's a two-way conversation.","tone":"good","next":"n2","reply":"Okay. Good.","feedback":{"en":"Purpose and structure first: it lowers stress.","tr":"Önce amaç ve yapı: stresi azaltır.","fa":"اول هدف و ساختار جلسه را گفتی؛ همین استرس را کم می‌کند."}},{"text":"Yes. Let's see if you passed.","tone":"poor","next":"n1","reply":"(He goes very still.) Did I... fail something?","feedback":{"en":"It sounds like a test he can fail. Open with the purpose and the parts of the meeting.","tr":"Kalabileceği bir sınav gibi duruyor. Amaç ve toplantının aşamalarıyla aç.","fa":"این جمله جلسه را شبیه امتحانی می‌کند که ممکن است در آن رد شود. با هدف و بخش‌های جلسه شروع کن."}},{"text":"Yes. Let's start with the problems.","tone":"ok","next":"n2","reply":"Oh. Okay.","feedback":{"en":"Starting with problems makes people defensive. Achievements usually come first.","tr":"Sorunlarla başlamak insanları savunmaya iter. Başarılar genellikle önce gelir.","fa":"وقتی با مشکلات شروع کنی، طرف حالت دفاعی می‌گیرد. معمولاً اول از دستاوردها حرف می‌زنند."}}]},"n2":{"speaker":"Deniz","line":"So... how did I do?","choices":[{"text":"Since April you've completed 410 deliveries, and your late deliveries have gone down from six a month to one in September.","tone":"good","next":"n3","reply":"(He smiles.) One in September. I didn't know that.","feedback":{"en":"Specific achievements with numbers, in the present perfect.","tr":"Present perfect ile, sayılarla somut başarılar.","fa":"دستاوردهای مشخص، با عدد و در زمان حال کامل. عالی است."}},{"text":"Fine, I think. No complaints.","tone":"poor","next":"n2","reply":"Oh... okay. (He looks disappointed.)","feedback":{"en":"Vague praise tells him nothing. Give achievements with numbers.","tr":"Belirsiz övgü ona hiçbir şey söylemez. Başarıları sayılarla ver.","fa":"تعریف کلی هیچ اطلاعاتی به او نمی‌دهد. دستاوردها را با عدد بگو."}},{"text":"You've done really well!","tone":"ok","next":"n2","reply":"Thank you... in what way?","feedback":{"en":"Warm, but he cannot tell what to repeat. Add the numbers.","tr":"Sıcak, ama neyi tekrarlayacağını bilemez. Sayıları ekle.","fa":"گرم و صمیمی است، اما نمی‌فهمد کدام کارش را باید تکرار کند. عددها را هم بگو."}}]},"n3":{"speaker":"Deniz","line":"Is there anything I need to improve?","choices":[{"text":"One thing. Although your paperwork is now excellent, your route reports often arrive a day late. If they came in on Friday, Omar could plan earlier.","tone":"good","next":"n4","reply":"That's fair. I can do them on Friday afternoon.","feedback":{"en":"One clear point, balanced with although, and the reason it matters.","tr":"Although ile dengelenmiş tek ve net bir nokta ve neden önemli olduğu.","fa":"یک نکته‌ی روشن که با although متعادل شده و دلیل اهمیتش هم آمده."}},{"text":"Well, your reports are a disaster.","tone":"poor","next":"n3","reply":"A disaster? I... okay. (Silence.)","feedback":{"en":"A label, not feedback. Describe the behaviour and its impact.","tr":"Bu bir etiket, geri bildirim değil. Davranışı ve etkisini anlat.","fa":"این برچسب است، نه بازخورد. رفتار و اثرش را توصیف کن."}},{"text":"Nothing really. Maybe small things.","tone":"ok","next":"n3","reply":"What small things?","feedback":{"en":"Too soft: he cannot act on \"small things\". Name one.","tr":"Fazla yumuşak: \"küçük şeyler\" üzerine harekete geçemez. Birini söyle.","fa":"بیش از حد نرم است؛ با «چیزهای کوچک» نمی‌تواند کاری بکند. یکی از آن‌ها را مشخص کن."}}]},"n4":{"speaker":"Deniz","line":"Thank you. Is that everything?","choices":[{"text":"Almost. Now I'd like to hear from you. What has gone well for you, and what would you like to do next year?","tone":"good","next":"n5","reply":"Just keep driving, I think. (He hesitates.)","feedback":{"en":"An open question makes it a two-way conversation.","tr":"Açık bir soru görüşmeyi karşılıklı hâle getirir.","fa":"یک سؤال باز گفتگو را دوطرفه می‌کند."}},{"text":"Yes. Please sign the form and we're done.","tone":"poor","next":"n4","reply":"Okay. (He signs. He never mentions his idea.)","feedback":{"en":"Without his view you miss what he wants. Ask an open question.","tr":"Onun görüşü olmadan ne istediğini kaçırırsın. Açık bir soru sor.","fa":"بدون شنیدن نظر او، از خواسته‌اش بی‌خبر می‌مانی. یک سؤال باز بپرس."}},{"text":"Yes, unless you have any questions?","tone":"ok","next":"n4","reply":"No, no questions.","feedback":{"en":"A yes/no question is easy to say no to. Ask \"What would you like to...?\"","tr":"Evet/hayır sorusuna hayır demek kolaydır. \"What would you like to...?\" diye sor.","fa":"به سؤال بله/نه خیلی راحت می‌شود گفت «نه». بپرس: «⁨What would you like to...?⁩»"}}]},"n5":{"speaker":"Deniz","line":"Just keep driving, I think.","choices":[{"text":"That's fine. You hesitated a little there. Is there anything you'd like to try, even something small?","tone":"good","next":"end","reply":"Maybe... Hasan says I'm good at explaining things to new drivers. I'd like to help train them.","feedback":{"en":"You noticed the hesitation and made it safe to say more.","tr":"Tereddüdü fark ettin ve daha fazlasını söylemeyi güvenli hâle getirdin.","fa":"مکث و تردیدش را دیدی و فضایی ساختی که بتواند بیشتر بگوید."}},{"text":"Perfect. Then no changes.","tone":"poor","next":"n5","reply":"...Yes. No changes.","feedback":{"en":"You missed the hesitation. Invite him gently to say more.","tr":"Tereddüdü kaçırdın. Daha fazlasını söylemesi için nazikçe davet et.","fa":"تردیدش را ندیدی. با ملایمت دعوتش کن که بیشتر بگوید."}},{"text":"Okay. Think about it and email me.","tone":"ok","next":"n5","reply":"Okay. (He probably won't.)","feedback":{"en":"Kind, but the moment is now. Ask one more gentle question.","tr":"Nazik, ama doğru an şimdi. Bir nazik soru daha sor.","fa":"مهربانانه است، اما فرصتِ گفتن همین حالاست. یک سؤال ملایم دیگر بپرس."}}]},"end":{"end":true,"outcome":{"en":"You confirm that Deniz has passed probation, agree that route reports will come on Fridays, and write down his idea: helping to train new drivers. In lesson 5.4 you turn that idea into a plan.","tr":"Deniz'in deneme süresini geçtiğini onaylıyorsun, rota raporlarının cuma günleri gelmesinde anlaşıyorsunuz ve fikrini not ediyorsun: yeni sürücülerin eğitimine yardım etmek. 5.4. derste bu fikri bir plana dönüştüreceksin.","fa":"تأیید می‌کنی که دنیز دوره‌ی آزمایشی را با موفقیت گذرانده است، توافق می‌کنی که گزارش‌های مسیر جمعه‌ها برسد، و ایده‌ی خودش را یادداشت می‌کنی: کمک به آموزش راننده‌های تازه‌وارد. در درس ۵.۴ این ایده را به یک برنامه تبدیل می‌کنی."}}}},"writing":{"id":"c-hr-5-3-w","title":{"en":"Deniz's appraisal summary","tr":"Deniz'in değerlendirme özeti","fa":"خلاصه‌ی ارزیابی دنیز"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-3","type":"writing","difficulty":"medium","prompt":{"en":"Write the appraisal summary for Deniz's file (70-100 words): two achievements (present perfect), one area for development (although or however), his own comments, and the agreed next steps.","tr":"Deniz'in dosyası için değerlendirme özetini yaz (70-100 kelime): iki başarı (present perfect), bir gelişim alanı (although ya da however), kendi yorumları ve kararlaştırılan sonraki adımlar.","fa":"خلاصه‌ی جلسه‌ی ارزیابی را برای پرونده‌ی دنیز بنویس (۷۰ تا ۱۰۰ کلمه): دو دستاورد (با حال کامل)، یک زمینه‌ی قابل‌بهبود (با although یا however)، نظر خود دنیز و قدم‌های بعدی که روی آن توافق شد."},"model":"Appraisal summary: Deniz Aydin, 30 September. Achievements: since April Deniz has completed 410 deliveries, and his late deliveries have gone down from six a month to one. He has also finished the defensive-driving course. Development: although his paperwork is now excellent, route reports often arrive a day late. Employee comments: Deniz said he would like to help train new drivers. Next steps: route reports every Friday; Leyla will discuss a trainer role with Omar by 15 October. Outcome: probation passed.","frame":"Appraisal summary: ___, ___. Achievements: since ___ he has ___, and ___ have ___. Development: although ___, ___. Employee comments: ___ said ___. Next steps: ___; ___ will ___ by ___. Outcome: ___.","words":[{"word":"since"},{"word":"although"},{"word":"next steps"}],"minWords":70,"minSentences":6,"rubric":["Task done: achievements, development area, his comments, next steps, outcome","Organised: labelled sections","Language: present perfect for achievements; although/however correct","Tone: balanced and factual; his voice is recorded"],"rubricI18n":{"tr":["Görev: başarılar, gelişim alanı, onun yorumları, sonraki adımlar, sonuç","Düzen: başlıklar altında","Dil: başarılar için present perfect; although/however doğru","Üslup: dengeli ve olgusal; onun görüşü de kayda geçmiş"],"fa":["کامل بودن کار: دستاوردها، زمینه‌ی پیشرفت، نظر خود او، قدم‌های بعدی، نتیجه","نظم: بخش‌های عنوان‌دار","زبان: حال کامل برای دستاوردها؛ کاربرد درست although/however","لحن: متعادل و بر پایه‌ی واقعیت؛ دیدگاه خود او هم ثبت شده است"]},"portfolio":null,"parts":[{"t":{"en":"Two achievements","tr":"İki başarı","fa":"دو موفقیت"},"find":["since april","has completed","has also finished","achievements"],"sample":"410 deliveries since April; the defensive-driving course"},{"t":{"en":"One area to develop","tr":"Geliştirilecek bir alan","fa":"یک زمینه برای پیشرفت"},"find":["although","however","development"],"sample":"route reports often arrive a day late"},{"t":{"en":"His own comments","tr":"Kendi yorumları","fa":"نظرهای خودش"},"find":["he said","he would like","employee comments"],"sample":"he would like to help train new drivers"},{"t":{"en":"The next steps","tr":"Sonraki adımlar","fa":"قدم‌های بعدی"},"find":["next steps","will discuss","every friday"],"sample":"route reports every Friday; trainer role by 15 October"}]},"perspective":{"id":"c-hr-5-3-p","title":{"en":"Deniz after the call","tr":"Görüşmeden sonra Deniz","fa":"دنیز بعد از تماس"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-3","type":"perspective","minSentences":2,"prompt":{"en":"You are Deniz in the truck after the call, engine off. Write 2-3 sentences in first person: what did you want to say but didn't, and what stopped you?","tr":"Görüşmeden sonra motoru kapalı kamyonda oturan Deniz'sin. Birinci tekil şahısla 2-3 cümle yaz: ne söylemek istedin ama söylemedin ve seni ne durdurdu?","fa":"تو دنیز هستی. تماس تمام شده و در کامیون نشسته‌ای، موتور خاموش است. از زبان خودت دو یا سه جمله بنویس: چه چیزی می‌خواستی بگویی و نگفتی، و چه چیزی مانعت شد؟"}},"exit":{"id":"c-hr-5-3-x","course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-3","type":"exit","items":[{"from":"hr-5-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"___ the new route was longer, you never missed a delivery.","options":["Although","Despite","However"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"Although: a full clause follows (the new route was longer). 'Despite' needs a noun, and 'However' starts a new sentence.","tr":"Although: ardından tam bir yan cümle gelir (the new route was longer). 'Despite' isim ister; 'However' yeni bir cümle başlatır.","fa":"Although درست است، چون بعدش جمله‌ی کامل می‌آید. despite اسم می‌خواهد و however جمله‌ی تازه شروع می‌کند."},"hint2":{"en":"A whole clause follows the gap (the new route was longer). Which word joins a clause, not a noun, and can start the sentence?","tr":"Boşluktan sonra tam bir yan cümle geliyor (the new route was longer). Hangi kelime bir ismi değil, bir yan cümleyi bağlar ve cümleyi başlatabilir?","fa":"بعد از جای خالی یک جمله‌ی کامل آمده (⁨the new route was longer⁩). کدام کلمه یک جمله را وصل می‌کند، نه یک اسم را، و می‌تواند اول جمله بیاید؟"}},{"from":"hr-5-3","kind":"blank","prompt":"Since June you ___ three new drivers.","options":["have trained","trained","are training"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"have trained: 'since June' runs until now, so the present perfect. 'Trained' is for finished time, and 'are training' doesn't go with since.","tr":"have trained: 'since June' bugüne kadar sürer, bu yüzden present perfect. 'Trained' bitmiş zaman içindir; 'are training' since ile kullanılmaz.","fa":"have trained درست است، چون since June تا الان ادامه دارد و حال کامل می‌خواهد. trained برای زمان تمام‌شده است و are training با since نمی‌آید."}},{"from":"hr-5-3","kind":"mcq","prompt":"You have shown Deniz his numbers and one area to improve. Which line makes the meeting two-way?","options":["How do you see your role developing over the next year?","You're happy in your role, aren't you?","Next year I want you to lead the night shift."],"correct":0,"point":1,"why":{"en":"'How do you see your role developing over the next year?' is an open question about his own plans, so he does the talking and the meeting is two-way. The tag question only waits for a yes, and 'I want you to lead...' decides for him.","tr":"'How do you see your role developing over the next year?' onun kendi planlarını soran açık uçlu bir soru; böylece konuşan o olur ve görüşme karşılıklı hâle gelir. Onay sorusu (question tag) yalnızca bir 'evet' bekler; 'I want you to lead...' ise onun yerine karar verir.","fa":"«⁨How do you see your role developing over the next year?⁩» درست است: سؤالی باز درباره‌ی برنامه‌های خودش است، پس او حرف می‌زند و جلسه دوطرفه می‌شود. سؤال تأییدی «⁨You're happy..., aren't you?⁩» فقط منتظر یک «بله» است و «⁨I want you to lead...⁩» به‌جای او تصمیم می‌گیرد."},"hint2":{"en":"After the evidence, the employee should do most of the talking. Which line asks about his own plans and leaves the answer to him?","tr":"Kanıtlardan sonra konuşmanın çoğunu çalışan yapmalı. Hangi cümle onun kendi planlarını soruyor ve cevabı ona bırakıyor?","fa":"بعد از مدرک‌ها، بیشتر حرف را باید خود کارمند بزند. کدام جمله درباره‌ی برنامه‌های خودش می‌پرسد و جواب را به خودش می‌سپارد؟"}},{"from":"hr-5-2","kind":"blank","prompt":"This ___ that the client called Omar to complain.","options":["meaned","meaning","meant"],"correct":2,"point":2,"why":{"en":"meant: the past of 'mean' is meant. 'Meaned' is not a word, and 'meaning' is not a full verb.","tr":"meant: 'mean' fiilinin geçmişi meant'tir. 'Meaned' diye bir kelime yoktur; 'meaning' tam fiil değildir.","fa":"meant درست است، چون گذشته‌ی mean همان meant است. meaned وجود ندارد و meaning فعل کامل نیست."}},{"from":"hr-4-4","kind":"blank","prompt":"If we ___ your route, would that help?","options":["will change","changed","have changed"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"changed: 'If we..., would that help?' offers a possible change, so if + past. 'Will change' and 'have changed' don't go with would.","tr":"changed: 'If we..., would that help?' olası bir değişiklik önerir, bu yüzden if + geçmiş. 'Will change' ve 'have changed' would ile gelmez.","fa":"changed درست است، چون If we..., would that help? تغییری احتمالی پیشنهاد می‌کند و بعد از if گذشته می‌آید. will change و have changed با would جور نیستند."}},{"from":"hr-3-4","kind":"blank","prompt":"Unfortunately, the night route ___ to a more experienced driver.","options":["has given","has been given","is giving"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"has been given: the route receives the action, so has been + past participle. 'Has given' says the route gave something, and 'is giving' is wrong for news.","tr":"has been given: rota eylemi alır, bu yüzden has been + üçüncü hâl. 'Has given' rotanın bir şey verdiğini söyler; 'is giving' haber için yanlıştır.","fa":"has been given درست است، چون مسیر به کسی داده شده و has been و اسم مفعول لازم است. has given یعنی خود مسیر چیزی داده و is giving برای خبر غلط است."}}]}}; })(globalThis.COURSE_FILES = globalThis.COURSE_FILES || {});
